
<section class="nb-sec-tight" id="showcase">
  <div class="nb-wrap">
    <div class="nb-head center nb-reveal">
      <span class="nb-eyebrow">Real interface</span>
      <h2>The real interface, worked through.</h2>
      <p>Four screens from the shipping app, two of them filled in with an example account so the charts are not sitting empty. Every score, letter and figure on them traces back to the statute named beside it.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="nb-show nb-reveal" data-nb-showcase>
      <div class="nb-showcol">
        <div class="nb-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Product screens" aria-orientation="vertical">
          <button type="button" class="nb-tab on" role="tab" id="nbT1" aria-controls="nbP1" aria-selected="true" tabindex="0" style="--acc:var(--nb-violet)">
            <span class="tj">Win</span>
            <span class="tk"><i></i>CrowMark</span>
            <span class="td">Find tenders, draft answers, prove delivery.</span>
            <span class="tp" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="nb-tab" role="tab" id="nbT2" aria-controls="nbP2" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" style="--acc:var(--nb-sky)">
            <span class="tj">Qualify</span>
            <span class="tk"><i></i>CrowCyber</span>
            <span class="td">Cyber Essentials evidence in one place.</span>
            <span class="tp" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="nb-tab" role="tab" id="nbT3" aria-controls="nbP3" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" style="--acc:var(--nb-teal)">
            <span class="tj">Get paid</span>
            <span class="tk"><i></i>CrowCash</span>
            <span class="td">Overdue invoices priced to the penny.</span>
            <span class="tp" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="nb-tab" role="tab" id="nbT4" aria-controls="nbP4" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" style="--acc:var(--nb-lime)">
            <span class="tj">Qualify</span>
            <span class="tk"><i></i>CrowESG</span>
            <span class="td">One dataset, four reporting frameworks.</span>
            <span class="tp" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="nb-showfoot">
          <button type="button" class="nb-play" data-nb-toggle aria-pressed="false">
            <span class="sr-only">Pause the automatic product tour</span>
            <svg class="ic-pause" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="6" y="5" width="4" height="14" rx="1"/><rect x="14" y="5" width="4" height="14" rx="1"/></svg>
            <svg class="ic-play" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 5.2v13.6L19 12z"/></svg>
          </button>
          <span class="lbl" data-nb-status>Advancing every 6 seconds</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="nb-panels">
        <div class="nb-panel on" role="tabpanel" id="nbP1" aria-labelledby="nbT1" style="--acc:var(--nb-violet)">
          <div class="nb-frame">
            <div class="nb-chrome"><i aria-hidden="true"></i><i aria-hidden="true"></i><i aria-hidden="true"></i><span aria-hidden="true">app.crowagent.ai/crowmark</span><span class="samp"><i aria-hidden="true"></i>Sample data</span><span class="live" aria-hidden="true"><b></b>Live</span></div>
            <div class="nb-shot"><picture><source type="image/avif" srcset="/Assets/shots/dark/mark-analytics.avif"><source type="image/webp" srcset="/Assets/shots/dark/mark-analytics.webp"><img loading="lazy" src="/Assets/shots/dark/mark-analytics.png" width="2400" height="1600" alt="CrowMark analytics screen showing social value performance across a bid portfolio, scored against PPN 002" decoding="async"></picture>
              <div class="nbl" data-nbl="mark" data-nbl-from="nbl-tpl-mark" aria-hidden="true"></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="sr-only">Example figures on this screen, from a sample account rather than a live one: 22 total contracts, up 4 on the prior 90 days. Bid win rate 46%, up 7 points. Social value delivered £86,200, up £21,400. Evidence completion 75%, from 18 of 24 committed measures evidenced. Contracts by status: 3 draft, 4 profiling, 2 evidence, 6 won, 7 lost. Bids by sector: 9 construction, 5 facilities, 4 highways, 4 education. Monthly win rate: 25% in April, 50% in May, 50% in June, 67% in July. Average social value score: 62, then 66, 71 and 74 out of 100.</p>
          <div class="nb-pcap">
            <h3>Find the tender, draft it, prove delivery</h3>
            <p>Daily UK tenders from Contracts Finder and Find a Tender, answers drafted only from figures your own confirmed data supports, a PPN 017 disclosure on every draft and human approval before submission. After award, delivery evidence, PPN 002 social value at the 10% weighting, and s.52 KPI checks under the Procurement Act 2023.</p>
            <div class="nb-chips"><span>Find a Tender</span><span>PPN 017 disclosure</span><span>Procurement Act 2023 s.52</span></div>
            <a class="go" href="/crowmark">Explore CrowMark <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg></a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="nb-panel" role="tabpanel" id="nbP2" aria-labelledby="nbT2" style="--acc:var(--nb-sky)">
          <div class="nb-frame">
            <div class="nb-chrome" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>app.crowagent.ai/crowcyber</span><span class="live"><b></b>Live</span></div>
            <div class="nb-shot"><picture><source type="image/avif" srcset="/Assets/shots/dark/cyber-connectors.avif"><source type="image/webp" srcset="/Assets/shots/dark/cyber-connectors.webp"><img loading="lazy" src="/Assets/shots/dark/cyber-connectors.png" width="2400" height="1600" alt="CrowCyber connectors screen listing read-only integrations that supply Cyber Essentials evidence" decoding="async"></picture>
              <!-- Entrance only, and deliberately no worked example. This is the screen
                   where you connect a tenant, so "0 / 2 connected" and "Never read" are
                   not an empty account, they are the state before you connect one; and
                   populating it would mean rewriting the two Connect buttons, which
                   would stop it being the real interface. So the cards simply arrive in
                   sequence and nothing on the screenshot is altered. -->
              <div class="nbl" data-nbl="cyber" aria-hidden="true">
                <div class="nbl-cover" style="left:25.27%;top:25.41%;width:15.78%;height:6.21%"></div>
                <div class="nbl-cover" style="left:41.94%;top:25.41%;width:15.81%;height:6.21%"></div>
                <div class="nbl-cover" style="left:58.59%;top:25.41%;width:15.76%;height:6.21%"></div>
                <div class="nbl-cover" style="left:26.57%;top:41.23%;width:63.6%;height:5.15%"></div>
                <div class="nbl-cover" style="left:26.57%;top:47.28%;width:63.6%;height:5.2%"></div>
                <div class="nbl-cover" style="left:25.25%;top:56.4%;width:65.75%;height:12.6%"></div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="nb-pcap">
            <h3>Cyber Essentials evidence, from the tools you already run</h3>
            <p>Read-only connectors gather posture evidence against the five NCSC controls on the Cyber Essentials v3.3 Danzell question set. MFA on cloud admin accounts applies from 27 April 2026.</p>
            <div class="nb-chips"><span>Cyber Essentials v3.3</span><span>Five NCSC controls</span><span>Read-only access</span></div>
            <a class="go" href="/crowcyber">Explore CrowCyber <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg></a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="nb-panel" role="tabpanel" id="nbP3" aria-labelledby="nbT3" style="--acc:var(--nb-teal)">
          <div class="nb-frame">
            <div class="nb-chrome" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>app.crowagent.ai/crowcash</span><span class="live"><b></b>Live</span></div>
            <div class="nb-shot"><picture><source type="image/avif" srcset="/Assets/shots/dark/cash-forecast.avif"><source type="image/webp" srcset="/Assets/shots/dark/cash-forecast.webp"><img loading="lazy" src="/Assets/shots/dark/cash-forecast.png" width="2400" height="1600" alt="CrowCash forecast screen projecting cash recovered from overdue invoices over time" decoding="async"></picture>
              <!-- Entrance overlay. Counters land on the four figures printed on the
                   screenshot, the four bars grow to the weekly amounts behind them,
                   and the table rows arrive in order. Nine of the thirteen weeks are
                   genuinely empty and stay empty. -->
              <div class="nbl" data-nbl="cash" aria-hidden="true">
                <div class="nbl-mask" style="left:25.583%;top:26.5%;width:19.958%;height:2.75%"><span class="nbl-num cash" style="--dy:-.083cqw" data-nbl-to="3500" data-nbl-fmt="gbp2">£3,500.00</span></div>
                <div class="nbl-mask" style="left:47.833%;top:26.5%;width:19.917%;height:2.75%"><span class="nbl-num cash" style="--dy:-.083cqw" data-nbl-to="24270" data-nbl-fmt="gbp2">£24,270.00</span></div>
                <div class="nbl-mask" style="left:70.042%;top:26.5%;width:19.958%;height:2.75%"><span class="nbl-num cash" style="--dy:-.083cqw" data-nbl-to="24270" data-nbl-fmt="gbp2">£24,270.00</span></div>
                <div class="nbl-mask" style="left:25.583%;top:48.625%;width:19.958%;height:2.625%"><span class="nbl-num cash" data-nbl-to="8118" data-nbl-fmt="gbp2">£8,118.00</span></div>
                <div class="nbl-mask" style="left:31.458%;top:74.438%;width:2.417%;height:3.813%"><i class="nbl-bar teal"></i></div>
                <div class="nbl-mask" style="left:36%;top:71.438%;width:2.417%;height:6.813%"><i class="nbl-bar teal"></i></div>
                <div class="nbl-mask" style="left:40.542%;top:76.875%;width:2.417%;height:1.375%"><i class="nbl-bar teal"></i></div>
                <div class="nbl-mask" style="left:45.083%;top:63.563%;width:2.417%;height:14.688%"><i class="nbl-bar teal"></i></div>
                <div class="nbl-cover" style="left:25%;top:25.375%;width:21.125%;height:6.5%"></div>
                <div class="nbl-cover" style="left:47.25%;top:25.375%;width:21.083%;height:6.5%"></div>
                <div class="nbl-cover" style="left:69.458%;top:25.375%;width:21.125%;height:6.5%"></div>
                <div class="nbl-cover" style="left:25%;top:47.375%;width:21.125%;height:9.813%"></div>
                <div class="nbl-cover" style="left:47.25%;top:47.375%;width:21.083%;height:9.813%"></div>
                <div class="nbl-cover" style="left:69.458%;top:47.375%;width:21.125%;height:9.813%"></div>
                <div class="nbl-cover" style="left:25%;top:59.25%;width:65.583%;height:23.125%"></div>
                <div class="nbl-cover" style="left:25.083%;top:87.75%;width:65.5%;height:2.938%"></div>
                <div class="nbl-cover" style="left:25.083%;top:90.813%;width:65.5%;height:2.938%"></div>
                <div class="nbl-cover" style="left:25.083%;top:93.875%;width:65.5%;height:2.938%"></div>
                <div class="nbl-cover" style="left:25.083%;top:96.938%;width:65.5%;height:2.938%"></div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="sr-only">Figures on this screen: £3,500.00 expected this week, £24,270.00 expected over 4 weeks including this week, and £24,270.00 expected over 13 weeks. Expected receivables run-rate £8,118.00. Weekly expected inflow: week of 18 July, 1 invoice, £5,000.00 gross due, £3,500.00 expected; week of 25 July, 2 invoices, £8,870.00 gross due, £6,209.00 expected; week of 1 August, 2 invoices, £1,841.00 gross due, £1,288.00 expected; week of 8 August, 5 invoices, £18,961.00 gross due, £13,273.00 expected. Nothing is expected in the nine weeks after that.</p>
          <div class="nb-pcap">
            <h3>Overdue invoices, priced to the penny</h3>
            <p>Statutory interest at Bank of England base plus 8%, with £40, £70 and £100 fixed compensation per invoice under SI 2002/1674, then a letter that quotes the Act back to the debtor.</p>
            <div class="nb-chips"><span>Late Payment Act 1998</span><span>SI 2002/1674</span><span>Base plus 8%</span></div>
            <a class="go" href="/crowcash">Explore CrowCash <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg></a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="nb-panel" role="tabpanel" id="nbP4" aria-labelledby="nbT4" style="--acc:var(--nb-lime)">
          <div class="nb-frame">
            <div class="nb-chrome"><i aria-hidden="true"></i><i aria-hidden="true"></i><i aria-hidden="true"></i><span aria-hidden="true">app.crowagent.ai/crowesg</span><span class="samp"><i aria-hidden="true"></i>Sample data</span><span class="live" aria-hidden="true"><b></b>Live</span></div>
            <div class="nb-shot"><picture><source type="image/avif" srcset="/Assets/shots/dark/esg-reports.avif"><source type="image/webp" srcset="/Assets/shots/dark/esg-reports.webp"><img loading="lazy" src="/Assets/shots/dark/esg-reports.png" width="2400" height="1600" alt="CrowESG reports screen showing one emissions dataset output across several reporting frameworks" decoding="async"></picture>
              <!-- Worked-example overlay. The account behind this screen has confirmed
                   nothing, so the whole scorecard reads 0% and every score is a dash.
                   The example puts 9 of the 19 VSME Basic datapoints confirmed, which
                   is the 47% completion, leaves 10 open across the five sections
                   (2 + 2 + 3 + 2 + 1), and scores 61 / 68 / 55 for an overall 61.
                   Carbon and materiality stay unstarted, which is what 9 of 19 means. -->
              <div class="nbl" data-nbl="esg" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg class="nbl-svg" viewBox="0 0 2400 1600" preserveAspectRatio="none" focusable="false">
                  <rect class="fill-card" x="612.5" y="400" width="170" height="32"/>
                  <rect class="fill-card" x="840" y="400" width="170" height="32"/>
                  <rect class="fill-card" x="1067" y="400" width="170" height="32"/>
                  <rect class="fill-card" x="1294.5" y="400" width="170" height="32"/>
                  <rect class="fill-card" x="1522" y="400" width="170" height="32"/>
                  <rect class="fill-page" x="773" y="519" width="17" height="21"/>
                  <rect class="fill-pill2" x="2113" y="717" width="13" height="16"/>
                  <rect class="fill-pill" x="1642" y="832.6" width="16" height="18"/>
                  <rect class="fill-pill" x="1642" y="888.3" width="16" height="18"/>
                  <rect class="fill-pill" x="1642" y="944" width="16" height="18"/>
                  <rect class="fill-pill" x="1642" y="999.7" width="16" height="18"/>

                  <g class="fig esg" font-size="31">
                    <text x="620.5" y="428" data-nbl-to="47" data-nbl-fmt="pct">47%</text>
                    <text x="848" y="428" data-nbl-to="61" data-nbl-fmt="int">61</text>
                    <text x="1075" y="428" data-nbl-to="68" data-nbl-fmt="int">68</text>
                    <text x="1302.5" y="428" data-nbl-to="55" data-nbl-fmt="int">55</text>
                    <text x="1530" y="428" data-nbl-to="61" data-nbl-fmt="int">61</text>
                  </g>
                  <text class="ink" x="776" y="536.25" font-size="18" data-nbl-to="9" data-nbl-fmt="int">9</text>
                  <text class="amb" x="2116" y="730.4" font-size="13" data-nbl-to="9" data-nbl-fmt="int">9</text>
                  <g class="amb" font-size="15">
                    <text x="1645" y="846.6" data-nbl-to="2" data-nbl-fmt="int">2</text>
                    <text x="1645" y="902.3" data-nbl-to="2" data-nbl-fmt="int">2</text>
                    <text x="1645" y="958" data-nbl-to="3" data-nbl-fmt="int">3</text>
                    <text x="1645" y="1013.7" data-nbl-to="2" data-nbl-fmt="int">2</text>
                  </g>
                </svg>
                <div class="nbl-cover" style="left:25.113%;top:23.775%;width:8.583%;height:6.313%"></div>
                <div class="nbl-cover" style="left:34.408%;top:23.775%;width:8.583%;height:6.313%"></div>
                <div class="nbl-cover" style="left:43.946%;top:23.775%;width:8.583%;height:6.313%"></div>
                <div class="nbl-cover" style="left:53.367%;top:23.775%;width:8.583%;height:6.313%"></div>
                <div class="nbl-cover" style="left:62.896%;top:23.775%;width:8.583%;height:6.313%"></div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="sr-only">Example figures on this screen, from a sample account rather than a live one: 47% completion, with scores of 61 for environment, 68 for social, 55 for governance and 61 overall. The report draws on 9 of 19 confirmed VSME datapoints. Ten datapoints remain open: 2 under general information and policies, 2 under energy and greenhouse gas emissions, 3 under pollution, water and resource use, 2 under workforce and 1 under business conduct. Materiality, carbon and auditor review are not yet started.</p>
          <div class="nb-pcap">
            <h3>One dataset, reported to four frameworks</h3>
            <p>An EFRAG VSME 2024 baseline calculated with DEFRA and DESNZ 2025 conversion factors, then output across SECR, GRI, ESRS and ISSB without re-entering a figure.</p>
            <div class="nb-chips"><span>EFRAG VSME 2024</span><span>DEFRA / DESNZ 2025</span><span>SECR, GRI, ESRS, ISSB</span></div>
            <a class="go" href="/crowesg">Explore CrowESG <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg></a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

